+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 78d94a8570 (crbug 586878505), ported from the M159 merge
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 24-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0005`). **Not merged to 15.6
+upstream yet**: ported from the M159 merge 78d94a8570 (V8 15.9.128.38, bugs 590052667 and 586878505; cherry-pick of
+main 602aeed99c). Applied as is to 15.6.75.66 (one-line offset in `lookup.cc`). Severity not published.
+
+- `ObjectLookupAccessor` (`__lookupGetter__`/`__lookupSetter__`) skipped an `AccessorInfo` and kept walking the prototype
+  chain, and `LookupIterator::Next()` could carry a stale `state_` into `LookupInSpecialHolder()` on the next holder.
+  Together they let a page read accessors from another realm's global without the access check. Now an `AccessorInfo`
+  returns undefined (it shadows accessors further up, per spec), `Next()` resets `state_` to `NOT_FOUND` when leaving an
+  ordinary holder, `NextInternal()` has a release `CHECK_EQ(NOT_FOUND, state_)`, and `STRING_LOOKUP_START_OBJECT` is
+  unreachable there.
+- Checked: `Start()`, `Next()` and `NextInternal()` in 15.6.75.66 are the same as in 15.9.128.37; `builtins-object.cc` is
+  identical. The only callers of `NextInternal()` are `Start()` (after `LookupInHolder` and `IsFound()`) and `Next()`.
+  `lookup.cc` and `builtins-object.cc` are not touched by any other `patches/v8` file. Test `regress/regress-586878505.js`.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`).
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): mjsunit `regress/regress-586878505`, `es6/*`, `harmony/*` and `regress/*` (the new release CHECK).
+
